{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "blackout-grid-collapse",
  "main": "worker/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-01",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./out",
    "binding": "ASSETS",
    "html_handling": "auto-trailing-slash",
    "not_found_handling": "none",
    "run_worker_first": ["/ws", "/ws/", "/healthz"]
  },
  "durable_objects": {
    "bindings": [
      {
        "name": "ROOMS",
        "class_name": "RoomDurableObject"
      }
    ]
  },
  "migrations": [
    {
      "tag": "v1",
      "new_sqlite_classes": ["RoomDurableObject"]
    }
  ],
  "observability": {
    "enabled": true
  }
  // Sin `vars`: la clave maestra del anfitrión va como SECRETO — `npx wrangler secret put HOST_PASSCODE`.
  // Un `vars.HOST_PASSCODE` con el mismo nombre SOBRESCRIBE el secreto en cada despliegue (wrangler avisa:
  // "Configuration values (...) conflict with existing remote secrets"). Y sin secreto ni var, el Durable
  // Object no tiene clave y rechaza toda orden del proyector.
  // Desarrollo local (`npm run worker:dev`): copia .dev.vars.example a .dev.vars.
}
